summary is: {{ This is the summary of the conversation:
A 26-year-old woman presented to the doctor with a dry and itchy skin condition on her hands and arms that started a few days ago after swimming. The patient works as a primary school teacher and has been feeling stressed lately. She has no medical history of skin problems, but her father has asthma and her mother has hayfever. The patient does not smoke or drink alcohol. The doctor diagnosed the patient with dermatitis and prescribed steroid creams and emollients to treat the condition. The patient was also advised to take antihistamines if needed to relieve the itchiness. The doctor recommended that the patient come back next week if the condition does not improve. }}<|eot_id|>
